\date{2026-06-04}
\meta{dev-id}{DEV-FAB-001}
\meta{status}{own}
\meta{location}{222 Dore}
\meta{nozzle}{0.2 mm (fine) + 0.4 mm (stock)}
\p{Status: \strong{own}. Repair and fabrication support. The \strong{0.2 mm
nozzle} is the fabrication floor of the capture#{\to}print loop
([[bci-scan-connection]]): 0.05 mm head scans reproduce down to a 0.2 mm feature
size — enough for electrode holders, the OpenNIRScap optode grid, headband
clips, and tFUS phantom skulls. Finer than stock 0.4 mm, coarser than the scan;
the scan over-resolves what the nozzle can lay.}
